---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="Privacy information for Church Software UK, including current analytics, form and structured-data practices."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Privacy" }]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy notice</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p>Last updated: 25 July 2026.</p>

      <h2>Current site state</h2>
      <p>
        Analytics are disabled. Suggestions, listing corrections and supplier
        updates use public GitHub issue forms; the site itself does not receive
        or store those submissions.
        The site does not intentionally set analytics or advertising cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting logs</h2>
      <p>
        The configured production domain is served through Cloudflare, checked on
        25 July 2026. No responsible publisher or final privacy contact is
        configured, so the site is not ready for public launch. Routine hosting
        may process information such as
        IP addresses, browser details and timestamps for security and service
        operation.
      </p>

      <h2>Public contribution routes</h2>
      <p>
        Contributions are submitted to the project’s GitHub repository and are
        public under GitHub’s service and privacy terms. Do not include
        church-member, pastoral, safeguarding, financial or other sensitive
        information. Submit only public supplier evidence and, if needed,
        business contact details. Maintainers use submissions to assess factual
        corrections or research leads independently; a submission does not
        guarantee publication or a particular editorial outcome.
      </p>

      <h2>Public software data</h2>
      <p>
        The structured export contains publishable product information and public
        supplier-source URLs. It does not contain private editorial notes or user
        submissions.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices and questions</h2>
      <p>
        Do not use the public contribution routes to request access, deletion or
        other privacy action concerning data held by GitHub or a hosting provider;
        use that provider’s published privacy route. If a future responsible
        publisher or contact route is configured, this notice will be updated
        before public launch. Until then, please avoid sending personal or
        sensitive information through the project’s public routes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
